{
    "background_story": "Luna was a talented photographer with a passion for capturing the beauty of the world around her. However, her love for photography was constantly at odds with her rare condition - photosensitivity. Even brief exposure to sunlight would cause her skin to break out in painful blisters and rashes. Despite this challenge, Luna refused to let her condition hold her back. She adapted by shooting mostly at dawn and dusk, when the light was soft and gentle. Her unique perspective and creative use of shadows earned her critical acclaim in the photography world. Luna's determination and resilience inspired others with similar conditions, showing that with the right mindset, even the most debilitating limitations could be overcome. Her photographs became a testament to the beauty that could be found in the shadows.",
